Experiments on two machine translation tasks show these models to be superior in quality while being more parallelizable and requiring significantly less time to train.,1,Vaswani et al. (2017),finding,arXiv:1706.03762,Direct reported empirical finding on translation quality and training efficiency.
We show that the Transformer generalizes well to other tasks by applying it successfully to English constituency parsing both with large and limited training data.,1,Vaswani et al. (2017),finding,arXiv:1706.03762,Direct reported empirical finding on model generalization to constituency parsing.
In the former task our best model outperforms even all previously reported ensembles.,1,Vaswani et al. (2017),finding,arXiv:1706.03762,Direct empirical finding on beating existing ensemble models.
"We propose a new simple network architecture, the Transformer, based solely on attention mechanisms, dispensing with recurrence and convolutions entirely.",1,Vaswani et al. (2017),finding,arXiv:1706.03762,Core proposed architectural contribution statement of the paper.
"Our model achieves 28.4 BLEU on the WMT 2014 English-to-German translation task, improving over the existing best results, including ensembles, by over 2 BLEU.",1,Vaswani et al. (2017),statistical_result,arXiv:1706.03762,Quantitative empirical result with exact BLEU metric values and improvement margin.
"On the WMT 2014 English-to-French translation task, our model establishes a new single-model state-of-the-art BLEU score of 41.8 after training for 3.5 days on eight GPUs.",1,Vaswani et al. (2017),statistical_result,arXiv:1706.03762,Quantitative empirical result establishing state-of-the-art benchmark score.
